(MERIDIAN MARITIME - LEAVE POLICY \(SHORE STAFF\)) Tj T*
(Policy HR-101, effective 1 January 2026) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Annual leave) Tj T*
(Full-time shore staff are entitled to 24 working days of paid annual leave per calendar) Tj T*
(year. Leave accrues at 2 working days per month. Part-time staff accrue leave pro rata to) Tj T*
(their contracted hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Up to 5 unused days may be carried over into the next calendar year. Carried-over days must) Tj T*
(be used by 31 March, after which they lapse without payment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Employees in their probation period \(the first 6 months of employment\) accrue leave normally) Tj T*
(but may take no more than 5 days of leave during probation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Requesting leave) Tj T*
(Requests of 5 or more consecutive working days require at least 10 working days' notice.) Tj T*
(Shorter absences require at least 2 working days' notice. The line manager must approve or) Tj T*
(decline within 3 working days of the request. Leave is requested through the HR portal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Public holidays) Tj T*
(Shore staff receive 11 public holidays per year. The list of dates is published by HR each) Tj T*
(December for the following year. If a public holiday falls on a weekend, no replacement day) Tj T*
(is given.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Sick leave) Tj T*
(Employees receive 12 paid sick days per calendar year. Staff must inform their line manager) Tj T*
(before 09:30 on the first day of absence. A medical certificate is required once an absence) Tj T*
(exceeds 3 consecutive working days. Unused sick days do not carry over and are not paid out.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Parental leave) Tj T*
(Birth mothers receive 26 weeks of maternity leave on full pay. Fathers and partners receive) Tj T*
(4 weeks of paternity leave on full pay, which must be taken within 6 months of the birth.) Tj T*
(Adoptive parents receive 12 weeks of leave on full pay.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Bereavement leave) Tj T*
(Employees receive 5 days of paid leave on the death of an immediate family member \(spouse,) Tj T*
(partner, child, parent, sibling\) and 2 days for an extended family member.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Unpaid leave) Tj T*
(After 2 years of service an employee may request up to 30 days of unpaid leave in a calendar) Tj T*
(year. Unpaid leave must be approved in writing by the Director of the employee's department.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
